    "recipe": {
      "title": "All-Butter Double-Crust Pie Dough",
      "servings": "MAKES ENOUGH FOR ONE 9-INCH PIE",
      "prep_notes": "Freezing the butter for 10 to 15 minutes is crucial to the flaky texture of this crust. If preparing the dough in a very warm kitchen, refrigerate all of the ingredients before making the dough. The dough, wrapped tightly in plastic wrap, can be refrigerated for up to 2 days or frozen for up to 1 month. If frozen, let the dough thaw completely on the counter before rolling it out.",
